            "contribution_type": "addition",
            "exact_contribution": {
                "added": [
                    "#Exercise caution when operating power tools. Make sure that all of your tools have a three-pronged plug, and inspect all equipment for signs of damage. It is also important to turn off power tools before connecting them to electricity. Always keep power tools away from water, and clear the work area of flammable gasses, vapors, and solvents when tools are in use.<ref>https://www.osha.gov/sites/default/files/publications/osha3080.pdf</ref>[[Image:Prevent Electrical Shock Step 15 Version 2.jpg|center]]"
                ],
                "removed": [
                    "#Exercise caution when operating power tools. Make sure that all of your tools have a three-pronged plug, and inspect all equipment for signs of damage. It is also important to turn off power tools before connecting them to electricity. Always keep power tools away from water, and clear the work area of flammable gasses, vapors, and solvents when tools are in use.<ref> https://www.osha.gov/Publications/osha3080.pdf</ref>[[Image:Prevent Electrical Shock Step 15 Version 2.jpg|center]]"
                ]
            }
        },
        {
