                "added": [
                    "#Wear protective gear. Rubber soled shoes and non-conductive gloves provide a barrier. Putting a rubber mat on the floor is another effective precaution. Rubber does not conduct electricity and will help you avoid getting shocked.<ref>https://www.osha.gov/etools/electric-power</ref>[[Image:Prevent Electrical Shock Step 14 Version 3.jpg|center]]"
                ],
                "removed": [
                    "#Wear protective gear. Rubber soled shoes and non-conductive gloves provide a barrier. Putting a rubber mat on the floor is another effective precaution. Rubber does not conduct electricity and will help you avoid getting shocked.<ref> https://www.osha.gov/SLTC/etools/electric_power/personal_protective_equipment.html</ref>[[Image:Prevent Electrical Shock Step 14 Version 3.jpg|center]]"
                ]
            }
        },
        {
            "id": "32235681",
            "user": "WikiHow Horizon 3",
            "timestamp": "15:51, 25 January 2024",
