                    "To prevent electrical shock in your home, use 3-pronged plugs whenever possible and avoid overloading power strips or outlets. Store electronic devices away from the bath, shower, and sink. If an electric device falls into water, turn the power off before retrieving it. If someone you know is shocked, avoid touching them with your bare hands, since they could still be conducting electricity. For more tips, like how to stay safe during a lightning storm, read on!"
                ],
                "removed": [
                    "==Short Summary==",
                    "The best way to prevent electrical shock in your home is to replace worn or damaged equipment, like damaged cords or warm electrical outlets. Make sure you turn your home’s electric panel off before attempting to fix any electrical problems."
                ]
            }
        },
