            "exact_contribution": {
                "added": [
                    "#*To learn more about electricity and the cause of electric shock, read about it [[Master-Do-It-Yourself-Electrical-Safety|here]] or ask a trusted electrician.",
                    "#Find shelter. If you are outside and a storm approaches, quickly heading indoors is the only real way to be protected from lightning. Look for a completely enclosed shelter with its own electricity and plumbing, like a house or business. If that option is not available, hiding out in a car with the doors closed and windows up is also a safe bet. Covered picnic areas, stand-alone restroom facilities, tents, and other small structures will not keep you safe. No reliable shelter in sight? Reduce your risk with these preventive guidelines:<ref>http://www.publicaffairs.noaa.gov/grounders/lightningsafety.html</ref>[[Image:Prevent Electrical Shock Step 13.jpg|center]]",
                    ""
                ],
                "removed": [
                    "#*To learn more about electricity and the cause of electric shock, read about it [http://www.howstuffworks.com/electricity.htm here] or ask a trusted electrician.",
                    "#Find shelter. If you are outside and a storm approaches, quickly heading indoors is the only real way to be protected from lightning. Look for a completely enclosed shelter with it's own electricity and plumbing, like a house or business. If that option is not available, hiding out in a car with the doors closed and windows up is also a safe bet. Covered picnic areas, stand-alone restroom facilities, tents, and other small structures will not keep you safe. No reliable shelter in sight? Reduce your risk with these preventive guidelines:<ref>http://www.publicaffairs.noaa.gov/grounders/lightningsafety.html</ref>[[Image:Prevent Electrical Shock Step 13.jpg|center]]"
